This repository contains or is derived from the following third-party works.

1. robomimic v0.5.0 (third_party/robomimic)
   https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robomimic
   Copyright (c) 2021 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab. MIT License
   (third_party/robomimic/LICENSE).
   The copy is pruned to the Diffusion Policy algorithm and modified: a
   residual 1D-CNN noise predictor (SimpleConditionalResNet1D) and configurable
   UNet sizes; observation and action normalization of the validation set
   during training; `--resume` continuing the most recent run directory;
   depth observations counted as image observations when environments are
   created; and lazy loading of the language encoder.
   robomimic's Diffusion Policy implementation is in turn adapted from
   Diffusion Policy (C. Chi et al., https://github.com/real-stanford/diffusion_policy,
   MIT License).

2. Franka Emika Panda MuJoCo model (grace/envs/panda/assets/xml)
   From MuJoCo Menagerie, https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco_menagerie
   Apache License 2.0 (grace/envs/panda/assets/xml/LICENSE).
   Modified: the position actuators and the gripper tendon/actuator are
   replaced by seven joint torque motors (the fingers are not actuated);
   scene.xml adds mocap obstacle slots, goal/prior ghost bodies and
   visualization markers (all without contacts in the simulation).

3. Franka Panda URDF (grace/envs/panda/assets/panda.urdf)
   From franka_ros / franka_description, https://github.com/frankaemika/franka_ros
   Apache License 2.0. Generated from the xacro description with fixed fingers.

4. The planar obstacle layout (grace/envs/pointmass2d/maps.py) is adapted from
   the dense 2D environment of Motion Planning Diffusion (J. Carvalho et al.),
   https://github.com/joaoamcarvalho/mpd-public. Obstacles were moved and added
   for this work.
